The '''Syndulla residence''',<ref name="Hera's Heroes Gallery">{{SW|url=series/star-wars-rebels/heras-heroes-episode-gallery|text="Hera's Heroes" Episode Gallery}}</ref> also known as the '''Syndulla house''' or '''Syndulla estate''',<ref name="Trivia Gallery">{{SW|url=series/star-wars-rebels/heras-heroes-trivia-gallery|text="Hera's Heroes" Trivia Gallery}}</ref> was the home of the [[Syndulla clan]] located in the [[Tann Province]] on the [[planet]] [[Ryloth]]. Built inside of a [[mountain]], the residence had a front door open to a gated courtyard with two balconies above. The home also contained storage cellars and an office used by [[Cham Syndulla]]. Due to Cham's resistance against the [[Galactic Empire]], [[Imperial Military|Imperial forces]] occupied the home<ref name="Hera's Heroes" /> on at least two separate occasions during the [[Imperial Era]].<ref name="Rescue on Ryloth">{{TBB|Rescue on Ryloth (episode)}}</ref> Cham's daughter [[Hera Syndulla|Hera]] eventually blew up the residence after being [[Second mission to Ryloth|captured]] by [[Grand Admiral]] [[Mitth'raw'nuruodo|Thrawn]] while attempting to retrieve the family [[Syndulla Kalikori|Kalikori]].<ref name="Hera's Heroes" />

==Description==
Located on the [[Outer Rim Territories|Outer Rim]] [[planet]] [[Ryloth]], the Syndulla residence<ref name="Hera's Heroes Gallery" /> was the home of the [[Syndulla clan]]. Found in a [[region]] known as the [[Tann Province]], the home was constructed inside of a large [[mountain]] that appeared to rise and tower above the surrounding [[desert]] plains.<ref name="Syndulla Residence">{{Databank|syndulla-residence|Syndulla Residence}}</ref> The front entrance opened into a large, open courtyard, the [[stone]] base of which was inlaid with an elaborate circular pattern. The courtyard was surrounded by a solid stone wall with vertical stone posts situated at intervals along its length. Entry into the courtyard space was accessed via two arches along the wall, each of which was flanked by a pair of barred windows.<ref name="Devil's Deal">{{TBB|Devil's Deal}}</ref> The wreckage of a [[Galactic Republic|Republic]] [[BTL-B Y-wing starfighter/bomber|Y-wing starfighter]] sat in the courtyard some distance away from the gates.<ref name="Hera's Heroes" />

The home's exterior facade featured two balconies, the lower of which was supported by brown square-shaped columns, and this design was replicated along the balcony railings as low stone posts.<ref name="Devil's Deal" /> Along each balcony, an intricately-carved design was visible from the outside. Atop a small flight of seven steps,<ref name="Rescue on Ryloth" /> the main entrance was a set of brown sliding doors underneath an archway.<ref name="Hera's Heroes" />

Inside the Syndulla residence, the main entry room was an open rectangular space with a central area that was set two steps lower into the floor. The floor's design was geometrically segmented into squares of ornamentation.<ref name="Syndulla Residence" /> A pair of brown sliding doors were set across the room, on axis with the entry doors, and the room was symmetrical across this axis. Both doors were flanked by tall potted [[plant]]s, and several slender columns were situated around the room's perimeter. Two sets of four tall screens bordered the lower area of the room, and they emitted a soft blue light which was diffused onto nearby surfaces. Aside from this, the space was dimly lit by overhead lights from the tall ceiling.<ref name="Hera's Heroes" />

